Requirements
Requirement	Module	Access program	Statement
hooks.1	hooks	hook	Each hook event MUST be run by a harness's command hook as the void-os command with the event, as that harness names it, as its operand: a session's start, a subagent's start, a prompt submitted, a tool call succeeded, a subagent's finish, and the model's finish.
hooks.2	hooks	hook	The input's name MUST be the resolved pathname of the place the harness reports: the environment variable harness variables names for place, where it is set; else the first member harness members names for place, in that relation's order, that the hook input holds; else the working directory the hook is handed.
hooks.3	hooks	hook	The context MUST be composed before the hook input is inserted, so that a hook never gives back its own input.
hooks.5	hooks	hook	A hook input that JSON text rejects, or that the converter rejects, MUST end the hook as non-conforming, nothing being written on standard output.
hooks.6	hooks	hook	A data bank that cannot keep or give what it stores MUST end the hook as keeping failed, nothing being written on standard output.
hooks.7	hooks	hook	The hook input MUST be read whole from standard input as one JSON text, before the context is composed.
hooks.8	hooks	hook	The answer hook output's context gives MUST be written on standard output in UTF-8, and nothing where it gives nothing.
hook-input.2	hook input	insert	The hook input MUST be inserted into the data bank as one value of the input, its module specification the Value hook input schema, on the event the command is run with.
hook-output.7	hook output	context	An event answer members or context members gives MUST be answered as one JSON object holding, at each pointer answer members gives that event, its value, and at the pointer context members gives it, the context.
hook-output.8	hook output	context	An event neither answer members nor context members gives MUST be answered by nothing.
hook-output.1	hook output	context	On an event context members gives, the context MUST be, where the event begins the context, the data bank's names, then what is new of the input to the session and agent the hook input names, each by the first member harness members names for it, in that relation's order, that the hook input holds, less the values whose hook input names the same session and agent, each value then its records of _stored, as many whole values as the Value context limit holds.
hook-output.4	hook output	context	What is new beyond the Value context limit MUST be cut to the last whole values it holds, every value still being marked communicated and remaining readable through the data bank.
hook-output.5	hook output	context	On every other event, the context MUST be empty.
hook-output.6	hook output	context	The context MUST be MTSV text written by the generator.
